<PracticeSet />

<AtTheTable>
  At showdown, lay out each player's strongest five and compare only those
  cards. During betting, identify who still acts behind you. Position changes
  the information available when you decide; being on the button does not
  physically change the deck or guarantee the winning hand.
</AtTheTable>

<QuantCorner>
  A consistent ranking rule resembles a clear rule for comparing trade outcomes:
  decide which quantities matter before seeing the result. Position is an
  information advantage, much as observing a price update before acting changes
  the information available to a trader. It does not erase uncertainty about the
  next outcome.
</QuantCorner>
